    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:936a34ccc6e7c635",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "08fc1379dc09e440fae4eda0434e73f14cd422404d962bd5b813c9e8eddd784f",
      "text": "An early start to watch the sunrise at the El Tatio geysers, at more than 4,000 metres: their name means “the crying old man” in the language of the region’s original inhabitants. Between 6 and 7 am, dozens of fumaroles release columns of steam and boiling water against the blue sky; an outdoor breakfast warms you up, as temperatures often drop below −2 °C. On the way back, look out for vicuñas and viscachas and stop at Machuca, a tiny Atacameño village of adobe, straw and cactus-wood houses offering Andean crafts and local dishes. Transfer to Calama for your flight to Santiago and to the hotel.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_aligned",
        "fileId": "1ZL0KyYvLLXKgj6FssZ-poR-LXjew42px",
        "documentSha256": "634fdbcaa6a57ae7477a290d5e564a90ed5c304f99e9b1a602084cc7c3bec8d2",
